# Messages for customers.profiles, a COMPACTED topic.
#
# Compaction means Kafka keeps only the newest value for each key. Several keys below appear more
# than once on purpose, so the topic is a small history that Kafka is entitled to collapse at any
# moment: browse it and you may see every version, or only the last one per key, depending on
# whether the log cleaner has run. That is exactly what a compacted topic looks like in production
# and it is worth a newcomer seeing it.
#
# The last line is a TOMBSTONE: a key with an empty value. In a compacted topic that means "this
# key is deleted". A message browser has to render it as absence, not as an empty string, so the
# quickstart contains one.
#mode: key-value

